# Copy to .env.local and fill in.
#
# Storage: with BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN set, sessions + party rooms live in a
# private Vercel Blob store; without it they fall back to the gitignored local
# data/ directory (dev). Do NOT rely on the filesystem in production — Vercel's
# FS is read-only.
#
# Vercel deploy (recommended setup):
#   1. Create a PRIVATE Blob store in the Vercel dashboard and connect it to
#      this project. Vercel then injects BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN automatically;
#      copy it here too if you want the same store when running locally.
#   2. Add AUTH_SECRET (and COOKIE_SECURE=true) as project env vars in the
#      Vercel dashboard. .env.local is NOT uploaded.
# BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=
# AUTH_SECRET=32+ random characters
# COOKIE_SECURE=true  (only needed off Vercel: Vercel HTTPS deploys default
# to Secure cookies; set COOKIE_SECURE=false only for plain-http dev if the
# browser ever refuses to store the session cookie)

# Party Rooms (Razorpay)
# Without these keys the room flow runs in TEST MODE: "Pay" auto-approves so
# you can try the multiplayer room end-to-end for free.
# With keys set (use Razorpay dashboard TEST keys), checkout opens and payments
# are verified server-side. Room price defaults to ₹20/ticket; override with
# ROOM_TICKET_PRICE (INR, e.g. 20 or 25.5).
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# ROOM_TICKET_PRICE=20

# AI announcer (room chat bot). Without keys the bot answers from canned
# responses; with OPENAI_API_KEY (or AI_BASE_URL pointing at any OpenAI-compatible
# endpoint, e.g. a local Ollama or Groq) @bot and /commands use a live LLM.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# AI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini
